Subject: [PATCH] webrtc: answer the given address after a round trip through the proxy

The server-reflexive candidate gathered for --fingerprint-webrtc-ip came
20 to 60 ms after the binding request. A host at the proxy's address
cannot hear from a STUN server sooner than a round trip through the
proxy, and WHOX measured the answer faster than its own TCP round trip
to that address.

The renderer now passes the allocator the round trip the browser already
timed loading the frame's document, or the nearest ancestor document in
its process: the TLS handshake or the wait for the response headers,
whichever was shorter, both made through the proxy. The synthetic STUN
answer comes after that round trip, capped at a second, plus up to a
sixteenth of it as jitter; without a timed load, after 90 to 160 ms.
Candidates keep their order and gathering still completes after the
server-reflexive candidate. Nothing new is sent: no UDP leaves the
machine and no request is made to time the proxy.

